# Tutorly Console — routing for the Playables proxy (public/play.php).
#
# The proxy is addressed by PATH:
#     /tutorly-games/adult/console/play.php/<buildHost>/<path/inside/build>
# because a Unity build fetches its parts with relative URLs, and keeping the
# build host in the path is what makes those relative fetches come back to PHP.
#
# Apache passes that path to PHP as PATH_INFO in the default configuration, and
# play.php reads it. This rule is the safety net for hosts configured with
# `AcceptPathInfo Off`: it hands PHP the same two values through the query string.
# The visible URL never changes, so relative references inside the game keep
# resolving to the proxy either way.
#
# Nothing else in the app needs a rewrite — the rest is a plain static export.

Options -MultiViews
AcceptPathInfo On

<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
  RewriteEngine On
  RewriteRule ^play\.php/([a-zA-Z0-9-]{1,64})/(.+)$ play.php?proxy_host=$1&proxy_path=$2 [QSA,L]
</IfModule>
